COMMIT_MSG.txt

# Eval/monitoring output
output/*

# ...EXCEPT the transcripts the metrics history is derived from.
#
# `docs/coach-metrics-history.tsv` and the dashboard are computed from these, so without them
# committed nobody else can regenerate or verify a single number in them — and the whole
# measurement history of the project lives on one laptop and dies with it.
#
# Cost measured 2026-09-18: 7.6 MB raw, 0.7 MB compressed (11.4x, the text is highly
# repetitive), plus ~13 KB per future run. Git compresses blobs the same way.
#
# Only the transcript is kept, not `review.md` or the other per-run artefacts, and only from the
# directories the history actually reads: `coach_review_v*` (the version series) and `matrix/*`
# (the model x opening coverage grid). Ad-hoc sweeps and smoke runs stay ignored — they are not in
# the TSV, so committing them would cost space for files nothing reads.
#
# Do NOT strip the `prompt` field to save space. It is 83% of a transcript and it is where the
# composed cause and the closing instruction live, which is what `cause_voiced_pct` and
# `lesson_conc_pct` read. Stripping it saves a megabyte and removes the ability to backfill any
# metric that looks at what we asked the model to do.
# The idiom matters: a negation cannot re-include through an EXCLUDED directory, so `output/`
# has to become `output/*` and the exemption is walked down level by level.
!output/coach_review_v*/
output/coach_review_v*/*
!output/coach_review_v*/transcript.json

!output/matrix/
output/matrix/*
!output/matrix/*/
output/matrix/*/*
!output/matrix/*/transcript.json
